---
import { step } from "../lib/data";

const z = step("zombie", "02-attack");
const offset = JSON.stringify(z.manifest.godot_offset);
---

<section id="agents">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Let your agent do it</span>
      <h2>An agent building your game calls PAGAN like a service</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        While you play-test, an orchestrator agent asks PAGAN for the art it needs, reads back the
        manifest and wires the sprite into the scene. <code>manifest.json</code> is the contract, so it
        works for any engine; Godot resources come for free.
      </p>
      <ol class="timeline" id="timeline">
        <li>
          <span class="who o">orchestrator → pagan</span>
          <code>write_asset zombie.model.yaml</code>
          <p>"Wave 2 needs an enemy: top-down, 8 directions, walk + attack."</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="who p">pagan → orchestrator</span>
          <code>{"{"}"ok": true, "errors": 0, "warnings": 0, preview: image{"}"}</code>
          <p>It looks at the preview, then calls <code>build</code>.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="who p">pagan → game</span>
          <code>sprites/zombie.png · zombie.tres · manifest.json</code>
          <p>{z.files.length} files, frame rects, 8 headings × walk + attack, pivot.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="who o">orchestrator → game</span>
          <code>Enemy.tscn: sprite_frames = zombie.tres, offset = Vector2{offset.replace("[", "(").replace("]", ")")}</code>
          <p>The zombie appears in wave 2.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="play panel">
      <div class="ground">
        <pagan-sprite step="zombie/02-attack" heading="sw" anim="walk" scale="4" label="The zombie walking in the game"></pagan-sprite>
      </div>
      <p>Wave 2 · <span>zombie.tres</span> · walk_sw</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import "../scripts/pagan-sprite";
  const tl = document.getElementById("timeline")!;
  new IntersectionObserver(
    (es, io) => {
      if (es.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) {
        tl.classList.add("go");
        io.disconnect();
      }
    },
    { threshold: 0.3 },
  ).observe(tl);
</script>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line);
  }
  .timeline li {
    padding: 0 0 18px 20px;
    position: relative;
    opacity: 0.25;
    transition: opacity 0.5s;
  }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: -6px;
    top: 6px;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    background: var(--line);
  }
  .timeline.go li {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .timeline.go li::before {
    background: var(--glow);
  }
  .timeline.go li:nth-child(2) {
    transition-delay: 0.7s;
  }
  .timeline.go li:nth-child(3) {
    transition-delay: 1.4s;
  }
  .timeline.go li:nth-child(4) {
    transition-delay: 2.1s;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .timeline li {
      opacity: 1;
      transition: none;
    }
  }
  .who {
    display: block;
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-pixel);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .who.o {
    color: var(--teal);
  }
  .who.p {
    color: var(--glow);
  }
  .timeline code {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .timeline p {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .play {
    padding: 14px;
  }
  .ground {
    background-color: #1d2f27;
    background-image: radial-gradient(#2c4636 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 12px 12px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 24px 0;
  }
  .play p {
    margin: 10px 2px 0;
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-pixel);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .play p span {
    color: var(--glow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
